###  https://w3id.org/smn/YearlingFreshwaterResidence
<https://w3id.org/smn/YearlingFreshwaterResidence> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                            skos:Concept ;
                                                   obo:IAO_0000119 "Beacham, T.D. and Withler, R.E. 2017, PLOS ONE 12(9):e0183713, pages 1 and 2, whose lake-type juveniles rear in nursery lakes for at least one year and whose river-type juveniles rear in the river environment for at least one year. The figure of one to two years for river-type rearing is from Gustafson, R.G., Wainwright, T.C., Winans, G.A., Waknitz, F.W., Parker, L.T. and Waples, R.S. 1997, Status review of sockeye salmon from Washington and Oregon, NOAA Tech. Memo. NMFS-NWFSC-33, page 20."@en ;
                                                   dcterms:source <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0183713> ;
                                                   rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://w3id.org/smn> ;
                                                   skos:altLabel "Yearling migrant"@en ;
                                                   skos:broader <https://w3id.org/smn/JuvenileFreshwaterResidenceDuration> ;
                                                   skos:definition "Juvenile freshwater residence of one year or more: juveniles overwinter at least once in fresh water before migrating seaward, and therefore carry at least one freshwater annulus on the scale."@en ;
                                                   skos:inScheme <https://w3id.org/smn/JuvenileFreshwaterResidenceDurationScheme> ;
                                                   skos:prefLabel "Yearling or older freshwater residence"@en .


